General_SiSo_Auto_LTE_PUSCH_Performance_Test_Model_Activation_Admin
    [Documentation]
    ...  Activates and validates results of LTE PUSCH Performance Test Model via admin API. Version for TDD and FDD radios.
    ...  Test result validation relies on timeReceived value and parameters name check in every frame of results.
    ...
    ...  :param int cell_id: (Mandatory) : Global cell id of tested LTE cell, e.g. 1. In case of pusch_format 1 and test on linked NB IoT cell (guardband or inband),
    ...                                    cell_id of host cell should be set, id of linked IoT cell must be defined as local_cell_res_id_nb_linked parameter.
    ...                                    In case of pusch_format 2 and IoT guardband/inband/standalone cell's ID can be passed as cell_id argument.
    ...  :param int/str pusch_format: (Optional) format of pusch performance test, possible values: 1 or 2, defaults to 1.
    ...  :param str reference_channel_number: (Mandatory for Pusch format 1) One of following LTE UL test models supported for cell configuration:
    ...                                     "A3-1", "A3-2", "A3-3",
    ...                                     "A3-4", "A3-5", "A3-6",
    ...                                     "A3-7", "A4-1", "A4-2",
    ...                                     "A4-3", "A4-4", "A4-5",
    ...                                     "A4-6", "A4-7", "A4-8",
    ...                                     "A5-1", "A5-2", "A5-3",
    ...                                     "A5-4", "A5-5", "A5-6",
    ...                                     "A5-7",
    ...                                     For 1.4MHz ChBw:    "A7-1", "A8-1",
    ...                                     For   3MHz ChBw:    "A7-2", "A8-2",
    ...                                     For   5MHz ChBw:    "A7-3", "A8-3",
    ...                                     For  10MHz ChBw:    "A7-4", "A8-4",
    ...                                     For  15MHz ChBw:    "A7-5", "A8-5",
    ...                                     For  20MHz ChBw:    "A7-6", "A8-6",
    ...                                     defaults None means parameter will not be set in pusch format 2 test.
    ...  :param str reference_channel_number_nb_linked: (Optional) Used in Pusch format 1, type of uplink test model for NB IoT cells,
    ...                                                 defaults None means parameter will not be set in test.
    ...  :param int rep_time_interval: (Optional) : reporting time interval (in seconds), range <0 to 4294967295>, defaults to 1.
    ...  :param int resource_block_offset: (Optional) : Used in Pusch format 1, resource block offset, range <0 to 99>, defaults to 25
    ...  :param int/str nb_subcarrier_index: (Optional for Pusch format 1, Mandatory for Pusch format 2) : narrowband IoT sybcarrier indes,
    ...                                      range <0 to 47>, defaults to None means parameter will not be set in test.
    ...  :param str measured_frc: (Optional) : Used in Pusch format 1, parameter required to start test model, one of the following: “nbLinked”, “both”, “1Dot92Mbps”,
    ...                            defaults None means parameter will not be set in test.
    ...  :param int local_cell_res_id_nb_linked: (Optional) : Used in Pusch format 1, configuration id of linked NB IoT cell (guardband and inband), defaults to None means parameter will not be set in test.
    ...  :param int/str inband_prb_index_ul: (Optional) : Used in Pusch format 1, narrowband IoT inband prb index for ul channel, range <0 to 99>, defaults to None means parameter will not be set in test.
    ...  :param str guardband_index_ul: (Optional) : Used in Pusch format 1, narrowband IoT guardband index for ul channel, One of following: “undefined”,
    ...                                 “plus4590kHz”, “plus6840kHz”, “plus9090kHz”, “minus4590kHz”, “minus6840kHz”,
    ...                                 “minus9090kHz” or None, defaults to None means parameter will not be set in test.
    ...  :param str nb_repetitions: (Optional) : parameter required to start test model on narrowband IoT cell. One of the following:
    ...                             “NBR_1”, “NBR_2”, “NBR_16”, “NBR_64” or None, defaults to None means parameter will not be set in test.
    ...  :param int nb_subframe_offset: (Optional) : narrowband IoT subframe offset, range <0 to 255>, defaults to None means parameter will not be set in test.
    ...  :param int reception_subframe: (Optional) : Used in Pusch format 2, parameter required to start test model, range <0 to 1023>, defaults to 0.
    ...  :param int exception_subframe: (Optional) : Used in Pusch format 2, parameter required to start test model, range <0 to 1023>, defaults to 0.
    ...  :param int reception_bundle: (Optional) : Used in Pusch format 2, parameter required to start test model, range <1 to 31>, defaults to 1.
    ...  :param int expection_bundle: (Optional) : Used in Pusch format 2, parameter required to start test model, range <1 to 31>, defaults to 0.
    ...  :param int tdd_spec_subf_conf: (Optional) : parameter required for TDD configuration, range <3 to 9>, defaults to 7.
    ...                                              Parameter is not taken into account in case of FDD configuration.
    ...  :param int tdd_frame_conf: (Optional) : parameter required for TDD configuration, range <1 to 3>, defaults to 1.
    ...                                          Parameter is not taken into account in case of FDD configuration.
    ...  :param str digital_output_type: (Optional) : Used in Pusch format 1, type of digital output, One of the following:
    ...                                               "BinaryHarq", "SerialAgilent", "SerialRs", defaults to "SerialRs",
    ...                                               defaults to "SerialRs"
    ...  :param bool enable_harq: (Optional) : Used in Pusch format 1, harq enabling, True or False, defaults to None means parameter will not be set in test.
    ...  :param bool enable_digital_output: (Optional) : Used in Pusch format 1, digital output enabling, True or False, defaults to True.
    ...  :param int timeout: (Optional) : timeout (in seconds) for test startup and termination, defaults to 90.

